WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.301
A blow to Putin.

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.335
One penny is

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.370
all it takes to buy

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.505
an entire Russian ruble.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.240
Russia's currency hitting a 17 month

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.142
low against the US dollar.

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:09.409
In fact,

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:10.210
the ruble has lost

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.545
nearly 40% of its value so far this year.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.713
And in Russia,

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:14.414
people are taking

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.016
notice of this milestone.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.283
Just look at this news ticker.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.251
This is from Sergei.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:20.520
It's a Siberian oil town.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.688
I noticed this Max Seddon

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:22.722
of the Financial Times,

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.190
a friend of the show, flagged it online.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.259
We verified it, geolocated it.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.293
Someone put in text

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.462
that reads, quote, 100 rubles to a dollar

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.097
Lost your effing mind.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.366
Putin is an expletive and a thief.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.135
OUTFRONT now, the U.S.

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:36.770
Treasury Secretary, Janet Yellen.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.838
And Secretary, I appreciate your time.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.540
And I wanted to ask you about the ruble

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.474
in just a moment.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:42.342
I wanted to begin, though,

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.510
of course, with the US

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.111
economy, where you're marking

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:45.745
the one year

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.247
anniversary of President Biden's

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:48.815
Inflation Reduction Act.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.283
It does come, though, as gas

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:52.385
prices once again are soaring.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.287
The average price of a gallon

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.656
of regular hit $3. $0.85.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.591
It is its highest level in nearly

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.126
ten months, up $0.28

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.961
from just one month ago.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:04.097
How worried are you about this, Secretary

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:08.468
Well, we have seen some increase,

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:10.804
partly because of the summer

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:13.573
driving season and global factors.

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.675
But gas prices are down

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.978
off their highs so for a dollar 20.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.681
So of course

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:24.284
this is an area of uncertainty but

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.854
we're certainly well off the highs.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:29.856
And more broadly,

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.392
inflation has come way down.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:33.460
Something that's

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.096
been a tremendous concern to Americans

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.865
over the last three months.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:42.102
Inflation, both headline and poor,

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:45.138
has been running just around 2%

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.941
So I think the inflation news has been

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.577
overall excellent.

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:52.245
Well, there is still risks.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:54.681
We've got a good, strong labor market

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:55.949
with unemployment

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:57.450
at a 50 year

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.986
low of three and a half percent

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.522
and the economy continues to grow.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.424
So, you know, as you point out,

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:06.793
the rate of inflation has been plunging.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:07.794
It's a fair point.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:08.361
Last month,

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:09.362
consumer prices were up

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:13.266
3.2% compared to July of last year.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.234
A year ago,

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.235
and you looked at the same thing,

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:17.670
July to July, prices were up 8.5%.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.204
So obviously,

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:20.573
it is a huge improvement, as you say.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:20.974
But but

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:21.841
the direction is still

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:22.742
a green arrow, right?

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:23.910
According to Moody's,

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.579
the typical household spent $202

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.781
more last month on the same goods

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.984
and services than it did a year ago.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:33.653
$709 more than two years ago.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:36.356
So the rate of inflation has plunged,

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:37.891
but prices are still going up.

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:38.992
And these are huge numbers

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.126
for American families.

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:41.094
It's real hardship.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:43.730
What do you say to those families?

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.664
Can you tell them that

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:48.201
prices will actually go down

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:50.770
So I don't want to say

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.839
that the level of prices will go down,

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.674
but I think inflation

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.743
will subside to rates

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:59.078
that are quite normal and

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.348
within the range that the Fed

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.584
is seeking to target.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:07.787
President Biden has worked with Congress

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:10.957
and within the administration to do

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.159
what we can to lower

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:16.162
prices and give Americans relief

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:19.065
and the inflation and Reduction Act

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:22.168
had many features to do that,

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:24.604
including cuts in health

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.606
insurance, premiums

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.241
in drug prices,

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:30.476
the cost of insulin was capped.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.812
It's $35 a month.

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:33.947
And,

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.317
you know, we're working oil releases

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:38.418
last year

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:40.920
from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve,

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:43.323
I think made a big difference to

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:45.692
the gas prices people had to pay.

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:47.961
But inflation remains a problem.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.296
That we're focused on.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.364
And on that front,

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.865
I mean, the economy is by far

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.100
the top issue for Americans

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.201
in this election.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.569
The latest CNN poll,

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:57.637
Secretary Yellen, shows

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.405
that 75% of Americans

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.507
believe the economy is in poor condition.

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.209
And maybe that's because,

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.110
again, even though

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.278
inflation rates have come down,

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:07.347
they are still paying more.

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:09.749
63% of people in this poll disapprove

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.017
of how President Biden

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.219
is handling the economy.

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:14.787
What do you say, Secretary Allen,

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:15.154
to the clear

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.289
majority of Americans

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:17.790
who simply do not believe

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.059
that the administration is helping them

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:23.096
Well, you

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:24.063
know, Americans

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.298
know best,

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:26.099
I think the best

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.434
their own personal finances.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:31.170
And it is important to recognize that

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.205
when they're asked,

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:34.374
how were they personally doing?

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:36.743
Over 70% of Americans

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:38.311
say that

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:39.512
they're very comfortable

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:41.648
with their financial situation.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:45.652
So they seem to perceive the economy

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:48.721
as a whole, as doing list

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.923
worlds in New York personally.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.126
But most Americans

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.093
feel good

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:56.529
about their own economic situation.

00:04:56.829 --> 00:05:01.467
And, of course, I'm here in Nevada today

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:05.238
to talk to people about

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:08.641
President Biden's economic plan over

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:09.976
the last year.

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:10.543
Are real

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:12.312
wages have been rising

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:14.914
in almost all sectors of the economy.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:16.215
And the biggest gains

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:16.683
have gone

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:19.952
to low income workers who have seen

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:23.189
a significant reduction in inequality.

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:24.824
The secretary, as I mentioned

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:25.892
a few moments ago,

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:27.393
the ruble hit a 17 month

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:28.661
low against the U.S. dollar.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.430
One penny is an entire ruble.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.264
That news ticker

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:33.499
in that Siberian oil town of Sagot

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.268
calling Putin out over it.

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:36.469
Who knows what happened

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:37.570
with those hacked into or not,

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:39.572
but there it was in Siberia.

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:42.008
100 rubles to a dollar Lost your mind.

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:44.243
Putin is an expletive and a thief.

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:45.311
Now, Secretary,

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:46.479
you have repeatedly said

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:47.880
that Putin's invasion of Ukraine

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.116
is a big economic negative for the world.

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:51.117
And here we are,

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:52.885
nearly a year and a half into the war.

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:53.720
How much impact

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.354
do you think it is

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:55.688
having now on Americans

00:05:58.491 --> 00:05:58.958
Well, it

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:01.561
continues to have impact on Americans.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.664
Beyond the money

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:07.467
that we're spending to support Ukraine,

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:09.335
The cutoff

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:10.903
of Ukrainian grain

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:14.741
from Russia's decision to in the Baltic

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:17.276
Green Initiative is pushing up

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:18.544
food prices

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.012
with the biggest toll

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.215
in the poorest countries of the world.

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:22.782
And it

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:25.017
continues to have some impact

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.786
on gas prices.

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:28.221
But as you mentioned,

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:29.522
the ruble

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:31.657
has declined in value,

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.693
which is a reflection of the fact

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.628
that our sanctions,

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:38.598
our program of sanctions with our allies

00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:39.932
and the war

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:41.934
is causing a drain

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:43.836
on the Russian economy.

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:45.905
So I want to ask you one more thing.

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:47.407
You recently were in China

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:48.841
you ate dinner at a restaurant

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:49.842
chain called In and out.

00:06:49.842 --> 00:06:51.210
And I should say to Americans

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.812
not to be confused with the burger joint,

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:55.248
I see you smiling.

00:06:55.248 --> 00:06:55.481
You set

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:56.048
off a frenzy

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:57.784
because you ordered a mushroom dish

00:06:57.784 --> 00:06:58.651
that contains

00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:59.852
apparently what are considered

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:01.754
magic mushrooms,

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:03.222
mushrooms that can be hallucinogenic.

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:04.857
And so now these wild mushroom

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:05.691
dishes are selling out

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:06.392
at that restaurant's

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:07.393
branches across China.

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:09.695
You have have sparked all this.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:12.031
May I ask you I'm just quite curious.

00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:15.001
What was it like, the mushroom experience

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.705
So I went with this large

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:20.973
group of people,

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:23.943
and the person who arranged our dinner

00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:25.812
did the ordering.

00:07:25.812 --> 00:07:28.080
There was a delicious mushroom dish.

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:31.984
I was not aware that these mushrooms

00:07:31.984 --> 00:07:35.254
had hallucinogenic properties.

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:36.956
I learned that later.

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:38.291
I could tell you later,

00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:39.792
like when you were sleeping

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:42.261
and having visions or

00:07:43.663 --> 00:07:46.466
really I was worried

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:47.667
that if the mushrooms

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:48.701
are cooked properly,

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:50.269
which I'm sure they were,

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:52.305
it's this very good restaurant

00:07:52.305 --> 00:07:54.073
that they have no impact.

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:56.442
But all of us enjoyed the mushrooms,

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:57.643
the restaurant,

00:07:57.643 --> 00:08:00.646
and none of us still felt any ill effects

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:03.249
from having eaten them.

00:08:03.249 --> 00:08:03.683
All right.

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:03.950
Well,

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.885
and now they're now they're selling out

00:08:05.885 --> 00:08:06.886
in and out China.

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:07.620
Well, Secretary Yellin,

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:08.621
thanks so much for your time.

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:09.288
I appreciate it.

00:08:11.257 --> 00:08:11.691
You bet.

00:08:11.691 --> 00:08:12.325
Thanks Erin.

